# CODEOWNERS for znasllc-io/memql
#
# Branch-protection on `main` requires code-owner review on every PR that
# touches a path covered here. Patterns are evaluated last-match-wins; keep the
# catch-all at the top and the security-sensitive overrides at the bottom.
#
# TEAMS, NOT INDIVIDUALS (memql#4463). These entries named a single account.
# GitHub does not let an author approve their own pull request, so a
# single-account owner makes that person unable to land a change to their own
# paths -- the protection becomes a block precisely when the owner is the one
# working, and the usual escape is an admin bypass, which is the protection not
# running at all. A team absorbs that: another member reviews. It also survives
# the org growing, which a list of usernames does not.

# Default owner for everything else.
*                        @znasllc-io/human-developers

# CI / workflows / supply-chain
/.github/                @znasllc-io/human-lead-developers
/.gitleaks.toml          @znasllc-io/human-lead-developers

# Auth + transport (security-critical)
/app/                    @znasllc-io/human-lead-developers
/component/identity/     @znasllc-io/human-lead-developers
/component/grpc/         @znasllc-io/human-lead-developers
/component/server/       @znasllc-io/human-lead-developers
/component/auth/         @znasllc-io/human-lead-developers
/component/worker/       @znasllc-io/human-lead-developers

# Build + deploy
/Dockerfile              @znasllc-io/human-lead-developers
/deploy/k8s/             @znasllc-io/human-lead-developers
/scripts/deploy/         @znasllc-io/human-lead-developers
/scripts/install/        @znasllc-io/human-lead-developers
/docker/                 @znasllc-io/human-lead-developers

# The shared capability-script runtime, and the allowlist that is the security
# boundary for the action path: a DSL action may only run a script registered
# there, so an addition widens what an automation can execute on the runner
# (memql#2221, memql#4463).
/scripts/lib/capability.sh                         @znasllc-io/human-lead-developers
/component/automations/steps/capability_script.go  @znasllc-io/human-lead-developers

# The operator-name ban list. Editing it is how a client-specific name would
# legitimately enter a company-agnostic repository -- which is to say, it should
# not happen quietly (memql#3593, memql#4217).
/core/vendorname/        @znasllc-io/human-lead-developers

# Auth-related docs
/docs/auth/              @znasllc-io/human-lead-developers
/docs/public/operate/auth/                         @znasllc-io/human-lead-developers
/SECURITY.md             @znasllc-io/human-lead-developers

# The instructions every agent session loads before doing anything.
/CLAUDE.md               @znasllc-io/human-lead-developers
